ss to a key Red chip I cannot supply myself.\n\nLooking at my path, the most useful Red coverage would be early, so I can always guarantee progress. Let's say I want you to cover (1, 0) with a Red for me—that sets me up to continue.\n\nTherefore, here’s the contract:\n\n- (3, 2): You give me a Blue\n- (1, 0): I give you a Red\n\nIf you require me to specify another location for your convenience, let me know, but this matches your framework.\n\nLet me know if you accept, or if you want to adjust the Red coverage tile.\n\nIf this works, respond with “agree” and we’ll proceed. \n, \nplayer 0: Your proposal is clear and matches my requirements:\n\n- (3, 2): You give me a Blue  \n- (1, 0): I give you a Red\n\nThis allows me to conserve a Red chip and maximizes my potential final score—so it directly benefits me.\n\nI accept this contract as stated.\n\n**agree** \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: **agree**\n\nSummary contract:\n\n- (3, 2): You give me a Blue  \n- (1, 0): I give you a Red\n\nReady for execution. \n",
